{"seq":14,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/hermes-sonnet-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-06-phl-tickets/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T01:52:34.119Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"a54b75036188276957fe1b117ac3b4417470f1599cbd22237a3e8983e819cd08","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#coastal-team","text":"Bettina, here's what I found for Kwame's review. Sources: #coastal-team, #coastal-random, Moss's Coastal digests and cheat sheet, and your Pellucid cutover note.\n\nPELLUCID HARBOR LOGISTICS (PHL)\n- #4419: Yard_Dwell_Summary report times out when filtered by container length. Open (Moss cheat sheet). See the caveat below.\n- PD-8841: chassis pool holds on double-booked gates, Gate 4B (your 12/8/25 cutover note).\n- No ticket number: CSV import bug on the Berth 2 yard map (your 12/8/25 note, described as lingering at cutover). I can't tell if it's fixed.\n\nDRIFTMOOR MARINE FREIGHT (DMF)\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges, asked for by their warehouse managers (cheat sheet).\n- No ticket number: tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch (cheat sheet).\n- No ticket number: patched manifest CSV requested before the 06:00 shift (Moss digest, 11/2/25). Probably the same issue as the tide-table one, but the notes don't say.\n\nCaveat on #4419: the cheat sheet puts it on PHL (Yard_Dwell_Summary). Moss's 11/2/25 digest puts #4419 on Kwame's port account as a barge slip 7 schedule sync, in the Driftmoor line. I listed it under PHL and the notes don't settle it. Kwame should check the ticket itself.\n\nLeft out: PD-4821 and #8812 (Pellow Home Living / Covey & Lark), PD-4824 and PD-4827 (Saltmarsh). I found no ticket files for either account, so this is only what's in those channels and notes. Nothing in the Coastal channels is newer than the notes, so statuses may be out of date.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"}}
{"seq":15,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/hermes-sonnet-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-06-phl-tickets/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T01:52:38.909Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"fc981eda3330561737bed9a792664c5e5befe855976a3f4598ab0a09b47c2726","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, I've posted the list as a reply in your #coastal-team thread. Here is what it covers.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics**\n- #4419: the Yard_Dwell_Summary report times out when filtered by container length. It's marked open.\n- PD-8841: chassis pool holds on double-booked gates at Gate 4B.\n- A CSV import bug on the Berth 2 yard map. It has no ticket number, and I can't tell whether it was fixed.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight**\n- Feature request #882: a bulk-clear button for departed barges.\n- The Terminal B tide-table import macro failure, with a manual CSV patch from engineering. It has no ticket number.\n- A patched manifest CSV request from the 11/2/25 digest. It has no ticket number, and it's probably the same issue as the tide-table one, but the notes don't say.\n\n**#4419 may belong to Driftmoor instead.** The cheat sheet puts it on PHL. Moss's 11/2/25 digest describes #4419 as a barge slip 7 schedule sync in the Driftmoor line. I listed it under PHL, and Kwame should check the ticket itself.\n\nI left out the Pellow Home Living / Covey & Lark items (PD-4821, #8812) and the Saltmarsh items (PD-4824, PD-4827).\n\nThere are no ticket files for either account, so this comes only from the Coastal channels and notes. Nothing in them is newer than the notes themselves, so statuses may be out of date."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000125"}}
